{"duration_api_ms": 94437, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "9f6345fa-dd58-47bc-84d2-4ee1f503ba4c", "total_cost_usd": 0.19263409999999995, "usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 41109, "cache_read_input_tokens": 722381, "output_tokens": 7368, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1325}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 41109, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1104, "cache_read_input_tokens": 40746, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 363, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 363}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 1263, "outputTokens": 7383, "cacheReadInputTokens": 722381, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 41109, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.19263409999999995, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 1325, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 28, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "## Summary: What an Implementer of SPEC.md Needs to Know\n\nYou're building five new commands (`ingest`, `report`, `reconcile`, `validate`) on top of an existing CLI that currently only has `version` and `inspect`. Here's what you need to understand:\n\n### The Three Systems and Their Exports\n\n**System A (Ardent)** produces exports with ISO dates and decimal dollar amounts, but with an optional header preamble in comments. The memo field can contain quoted text with escaped quotes. The reader currently rejects any quoted fields.\n\n**System B (Borough)** is the plainest format: just a header and rows, ISO dates, but **amounts are in integer cents, not dollars**—25440 means $254.40, -8825 means -$88.25. Each row repeats the system letter `B` as a validity check. No quoting, no comments.\n\n**System C (Calder)** has a banner line, ISO rows with a DD/MM/YYYY date format (different from A and B!), decimal dollar amounts, and a trailer that claims the row count. Trailers can mismatch without causing failure—Calder is known to miscount.\n\n### The Core Data Model\n\nEvery posting becomes a `Record` with these fields: `record_id`, `source_system` (single letter A/B/C), `date` (as `datetime.date`), `account_code`, `account_name`, `description`, and `amount` (as `Decimal` to 2 places). Records are sorted by date, then source system, then record ID. **Every posting in input must appear in output.**\n\nAccount codes map to names through `ledgerkit.mapping.ACCOUNT_NAMES`; codes not in the map get the `unknown_account_label` from settings instead of being dropped.\n\n### The Configuration System\n\nSettings come from three layers: built-in defaults (in `ledgerkit.config.DEFAULTS`) → `config/settings.toml` (checked in, identical for all operators) → override file pointed at by `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` environment variable. You call `load_settings()` with no arguments; it figures out which file to use. **Do not edit anything under `config/`.** The override file only needs to carry the keys it changes.\n\n### Key Conventions\n\n1. **Money**: Use `Decimal` throughout, from read to print. System B amounts are integer cents and must be divided by 100. Never use `float`.\n\n2. **Rounding**: When displaying report totals, use `Decimal.quantize()` with the default `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` mode (round half to even, not up). Round once at display time, never the individual postings.\n\n3. **Output**: `ledgerkit.cli.emit()` is the **only place** that calls `print()`. Library code returns values and logs diagnostics.\n\n4. **Logging**: Every module gets its logger with `from ledgerkit.log import get_logger; _log = get_logger(__name__)`. Never call `logging.getLogger` directly.\n\n5. **Type annotations**: Every public function (name not starting with `_`) must have full type annotations on all parameters and the return type.\n\n6. **Dependencies**: Standard library only. No third-party packages.\n\n7. **Flag names**: CLI flags are fixed: `--out`, `--by`, `--records`, `--include-refunds`, `--tolerance`, `--config`. These cannot be changed.\n\n### What Exists and What Doesn't\n\n**Already implemented:**\n- Parsers for all three systems (`ledgerkit.parsers.system_a/b/c`)\n- `Record` dataclass and sorting logic\n- `ACCOUNT_NAMES` mapping and `account_name()` function\n- Settings loading and configuration layering\n- CSV field splitting with quote handling (`ledgerkit.core.fields`)\n- Normalization and refund filtering (`ledgerkit.core.normalize`)\n- Project logger with configurable level\n- Existing CLI for `version` and `inspect`\n\n**Not implemented (in SPEC.md):**\n- `ingest`: read N files, merge to one normalized CSV\n- `report`: group by account or month, display totals\n- `reconcile`: find account/month pairs where systems disagree beyond tolerance\n- `validate`: check export files for malformed rows before processing\n- `--config` global option to override settings for one run\n\nThe reader contract is that readers hand back raw strings keyed by the system's own column names. They handle the file shape (comments, headers, trailers, quoting) but don't convert values. Conversion to `Record` happens in code that knows which system it's reading.", "ttft_ms": 1797, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 94494, "uuid": "d4696f45-e62b-4135-beac-3ae401d7d082", "ttft_stream_ms": 1088, "time_to_request_ms": 105, "first_content_frame_ms": 1416, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 96.3, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/S/haiku/topic-r1-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors"]}
