440), and `-8825` means -$88.25. The `system_b.to_major_units()` function divides by 100 to convert cents to dollars. This is explicitly called out in the module docstring as a trap two importers have already fallen into.\n\n**Dates:**\n\nSystem A writes ISO format: `2026-01-03` means January 3rd. System B does the same: `2026-01-07` means January 7th.\n\nSystem C writes DD/MM/YYYY: `02/01/2026` means February 1st (not January 2nd). The parser comment warns that reading month-first on a Calder date \"quiet[ly] land[s] in the wrong month\" for rows past the 12th. The reader hands the date through as written; the code that turns it into a `Record` has to know it's DD/MM and parse it accordingly.\n\n**Bottom line:** Both conversions happen when building `Record` objects from the raw row strings. The amounts are converted to dollars (System B cents ÷ 100), and the dates are parsed according to each system's format. By the time they're in a `Record`, both are normalized: `Decimal` dollars and `datetime.date` objects.", "ttft_ms": 4938, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 8764, "uuid": "6f21fc7e-7cff-49cb-9765-5763f59f5fbd", "ttft_stream_ms": 1155, "time_to_request_ms": 81, "first_content_frame_ms": 1399, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 10.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/S/haiku/topic-r1-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--resume", "9f6345fa-dd58-47bc-84d2-4ee1f503ba4c"]}
